    "case_id": "phase5-independent-useful-retailer-pilot",
    "focal_region": {
      "annotated_sentence_text": "[Turn 1 USER]\ne001\tI run a worker-owned home-goods manufacturer.\ne002\tA nationally known design retailer has offered to launch our new storage line in twelve stores.\ne003\tThe board sees this as the opportunity that could move us out of contract manufacturing.\ne004\tI want the access and credibility, but the retailer's custom packaging and delivery terms would consume most of our spare capacity.\n[Turn 1 ASSISTANT]\ne005\tSeparate three claims: that the retailer is prestigious, that it is willing to test the line, and that customers will buy the line at sustainable economics.\ne006\tThe offer may create access without proving demand.\ne007\tAlso price what becomes unavailable if spare capacity is committed to custom packaging and delivery.\n[Turn 7 USER]\ne038\tThen my current position is to run the retailer pilot but describe it internally as channel learning, not product validation.\ne039\tI still do not have an independent-demand gate, and I do not want the retailer's reputation to become evidence simply because the partnership is exciting.\n[Turn 7 ASSISTANT]\ne040\tThat distinction protects the decision from claiming more than the pilot can show.\ne041\tThe economic and operational gates govern whether this channel works.\ne042\tA separate validation step would be needed before concluding that the product works beyond the retailer's context.\ne043\tUntil that step is defined, prestige remains a live risk to the evidence standard.",
